WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Synthetic media is content generated or altered with artificial intelligence or related computational techniques.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.193
It can include images, video, audio, text, documents, and screenshots.

00:00:12.193 --> 00:00:19.645
Synthetic content may be creative, educational, assistive, misleading, or harmful depending on purpose and presentation.

00:00:19.645 --> 00:00:27.096
A deepfake is AI-generated or AI-altered media that represents a person, event, action, or statement.

00:00:27.096 --> 00:00:37.709
The term often describes face, voice, or motion manipulation, but analysts should avoid using it as a label for every suspicious file.

00:00:37.709 --> 00:00:43.805
Ordinary editing changes real media through cropping, color adjustment, compositing, or sequencing.

00:00:43.805 --> 00:00:46.741
Manipulation changes meaning or evidence.

00:00:46.741 --> 00:00:51.031
Fully synthetic media is generated rather than captured.

00:00:51.031 --> 00:00:58.934
Satire may be clearly signaled, while deception attempts to make an audience accept a false claim.

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:09.547
Real media can also mislead when staged, clipped, given a false caption, or presented as evidence of a different time or place.

00:01:09.547 --> 00:01:14.288
Verification therefore asks more than whether pixels were generated.

00:01:14.288 --> 00:01:20.837
It asks whether the claimed source, event, identity, date, and context are supported.

00:01:20.837 --> 00:01:26.030
Analysts need careful habits because intuitive visual judgment is unreliable.

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:33.030
Compression, poor lighting, frame interpolation, translation, editing, and platform processing can resemble synthetic artifacts.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:36.869
High-quality generation may show no obvious defect.

00:01:36.869 --> 00:01:42.062
The objective is disciplined assessment, not panic or instant certainty.

00:01:42.062 --> 00:01:52.675
Preserve the media and claim, investigate provenance, compare independent evidence, describe technical clues cautiously, and communicate what is known, unknown, and inferred.
